><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250704101200+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250704101215+10'00'" name="83f80891-3ce8-4a14-9346-502ca55b354f" page="1" coords="216.592010,144.259872,378.683044,144.259872,216.592010,133.459900,378.683044,133.459900,216.592010,133.081879,378.673309,133.081879,216.592010,122.281906,378.673309,122.281906,216.592010,121.903870,378.681946,121.903870,216.592010,111.103897,378.681946,111.103897,216.592010,110.725876,378.672607,110.725876,216.592010,99.925903,378.672607,99.925903,216.592010,99.547867,378.681000,99.547867,216.592010,88.747894,378.681000,88.747894,216.592010,88.369873,381.174988,88.369888,216.592010,77.569901,381.174988,77.569916,216.592010,77.191879,378.685364,77.191879,216.592010,66.391907,378.685364,66.391907,216.592010,66.013885,381.187622,66.013885,216.592010,55.213913,381.187622,55.213913,216.592010,54.835876,351.213684,54.835876,216.592010,44.035904,351.213684,44.035904" rect="216.254501,43.698395,381.525146,144.597382" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Sport governing bodies play a crucial role&#xD;in ensuring the health and welfare of their&#xD;playing population, which should include&#xD;investing in effective breast injury prevention&#xD;strategies. We call on governing&#xD;bodies of contact, combat and pseudo-contact&#xD;sports to invest in research and&#xD;development associated with evidence-based&#xD;breast protective equipment:&#xD;to evaluate the efficacy of breast protective&#xD;equipment in reducing the&#xD;severity and/or frequency of breast&#xD;injuries;&#xD;2. to verify that available breast protective&#xD;equipment meets user needs and&#xD;is not unduly burdensome for athletes;&#xD;3. to ensure that breast protective equipment&#xD;is physically and functionally inclusive&#xD;of the diverse user population;&#xD;and&#xD;4. to modify protective equipment regulations&#xD;as needed to facilitate safe&#xD;game play for all athletes. Such investment&#xD;will not only enhance player&#xD;safety and welfare but also help to&#xD;reduce barriers to the participation of&#xD;girls and women in contact, combat&#xD;and pseudo-contact&#xD;sports.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="1" rect="595.276001,52.259872,779.276001,144.259872"
/></highlight
